% chezmoi, dotfiles

# See what chezmoi would change
chezmoi diff

# Apply the dotfiles to this machine
chezmoi apply

# Pull from GitHub and apply
chezmoi update

# Edit a managed file in the source (then apply)
chezmoi edit <managed_file>

# Edit a managed file and apply when you save
chezmoi edit --apply <managed_file>

# Start managing a file
chezmoi add <file>

# Copy a live file's edits back into the source (e.g. after p10k configure)
chezmoi re-add <managed_file>

# Stop managing a file (keeps the file)
chezmoi forget <managed_file>

# Which managed files differ from the source
chezmoi status

# List managed files
chezmoi managed

# Where a file lives in the source
chezmoi source-path <managed_file>

# Open a shell in the source repo
chezmoi cd

# Commit and push dotfile changes
chezmoi git -- add -A && chezmoi git -- commit -m "<message>" && chezmoi git -- push

# Refresh externals (navi cheats, Oh my tmux) now
chezmoi apply --refresh-externals

# Health check
chezmoi doctor

$ managed_file: chezmoi managed --include=files --path-style=absolute
